From: qforge
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: route second-screen windows to the secondary output

NDS/3DS emulators put their second screen in a second top-level window
of the same process: melonDS titles it "[w2] ...", Azahar ends it with
"| Secondary Window". Both are plain, non-transient toplevels carrying
the game's STEAM_GAME, so gamescope showed whichever mapped last on the
main panel (Azahar), or the one OpenGamepadUI named in
GAMESCOPECTRL_BASELAYER_WINDOW (melonDS): the DS bottom screen on the
top panel.

With --secondary-output, a window goes to the secondary output when its
GAMESCOPE_OUTPUT property is 1, or, without the property, when its
title matches --secondary-window-title (default
"^\[w2\] |\| Secondary Window$"). Such a window is never a focus
candidate for the main output, which also keeps it out of
GAMESCOPE_FOCUSABLE_WINDOWS and out of a BASELAYER_WINDOW match, so the
main pick falls back to the game's other window. A separate secondary
focus picks the newest of them and sizes it to the panel (the panel's
orientation applied, as reported by IBackend::GetSecondaryOutputSize);
client resize requests on it are clamped to that size, and the desktop
window resize skips it. The secondary focus takes no part in focus
control: no appid, overlays or input focus.

Nothing is painted on the secondary output yet (next patch).

(qforge: dual-screen boards, step 3 of the dual-output plan, 2026-10-12.
Window shapes read with xprop on the Thor Lite: melonDS 1.1 with
Window1 enabled, Azahar 2126.1.2 with layout_option=4.)
